Compile gfx::D3DSharedFence under MinGW so the D3D shared-image pipeline
enabled by 0021 actually has its symbols at link time.

0014-chromium-ui.patch removed d3d_shared_fence.cc/h from the MinGW build
by adding them to a `sources -= [ ... ]` block under `if (is_mingw)` in
ui/gfx/BUILD.gn. With 0021 re-enabling the GPU side that calls into
gfx::D3DSharedFence, the resulting QtWebEngineCore link fails with:

    undefined reference to `gfx::D3DSharedFence::~D3DSharedFence()'
    undefined reference to `gfx::D3DSharedFence::CreateForD3D11(...)'
    undefined reference to `gfx::D3DSharedFence::CreateFromD3D11Fence(...)'
    undefined reference to `gfx::D3DSharedFence::CreateFromScopedHandle(...)'
    undefined reference to `gfx::D3DSharedFence::WaitD3D11(...)'
    undefined reference to `gfx::D3DSharedFence::IncrementAndSignalD3D11()'
    undefined reference to `gfx::D3DSharedFence::Update(unsigned long long)'
    undefined reference to `gfx::D3DSharedFence::GetDXGIHandleToken() const'
    undefined reference to `gfx::D3DSharedFence::GetFenceValue() const'
    undefined reference to `gfx::D3DSharedFence::GetSharedHandle() const'
    undefined reference to `gfx::D3DSharedFence::CloneSharedHandle() const'

Drop the d3d_shared_fence.{cc,h} entries from the MinGW exclusion list.
text_analysis_source stays excluded - it's an unrelated DirectWrite codepath
that has its own MinGW issues and isn't pulled in by the D3D pipeline.

mingw-w64 ucrt64's d3d11_4.h provides ID3D11Fence / ID3D11Device5 (the only
non-trivial dependencies of d3d_shared_fence.cc).

diff --git a/src/3rdparty/chromium/ui/gfx/BUILD.gn b/src/3rdparty/chromium/ui/gfx/BUILD.gn
--- a/src/3rdparty/chromium/ui/gfx/BUILD.gn
+++ b/src/3rdparty/chromium/ui/gfx/BUILD.gn
@@ -249,8 +249,6 @@ component("gfx") {
     ]
     if (is_mingw) {
       sources -= [
-        "win/d3d_shared_fence.cc",
-        "win/d3d_shared_fence.h",
         "win/text_analysis_source.cc",
         "win/text_analysis_source.h"
       ]
